":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","abstract":[],"title":"Cliques","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/adjacentPairs()":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/adjacentpairs()","role":"symbol","title":"adjacentPairs()","type":"topic","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"adjacentPairs"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AdjacentPairsSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Algorithms21AdjacentPairsSequenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\